* R131. A WORKSPACE OWNS ITS ENVIRONMENT (owner ruling 2026-08-29).
* Explicit-run until soaked. Self-bootstrapping in SANDBOX, self-erasing.
*
* WHAT CHANGED. The three path slots DBF, INDEXES and LMDB were GLOBAL, and
* WORKSPACE SWITCH moved MEMBERSHIP without moving them. So with two systems
* open, a table in one resolved its container under the other -- measured
* 2026-08-29 as MCC's STUDENTS answering
*   openCdx: LMDB env missing: ...SYSTEMS\CASCADE_ERP\LMDB\STUDENTS.cdx.d
* because Cascade had been opened last. Now the three slots are STAMPED on the
* workspace and SWITCH restores them.
*
* THE FIXTURE IS TWO TABLES WITH THE SAME NAME AND DIFFERENT CONTENT, and that
* is the whole trick. An arm that opens a table only present in one directory
* cannot go RED when the slot is wrong -- the open fails, the area is empty,
* and a marker over a closed area PRINTS NOTHING rather than a verdict
* (USE_AGAIN, three cuts). With RSPT.dbf in BOTH roots, a wrong slot opens the
* WRONG TABLE and the marker reads .F. A failure has to be able to speak.
*
* FIXTURE DIRECTORIES. DBF/SANDBOX/R131A and R131B must exist. They are EMPTY
* DIRECTORIES AND GIT DOES NOT TRACK THOSE -- the same standing gap WAOA/WAOB,
* OJCA/OJCB, PKA/PKB and RPCA/RPCB already carry. Inherited, not introduced.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131A
ERASE RSPT CONFIRM
CREATE X64 RSPT (ID N(4), MARK C(8))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "AAA"
CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131B
ERASE RSPT CONFIRM
CREATE X64 RSPT (ID N(4), MARK C(8))
APPEND
REPLACE ID WITH 1
REPLACE MARK WITH "BBB"
CLOSE
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
* GUARDS. Each fixture read ON ITS OWN, through its own slot, before any
* workspace exists. Without these an arm reading the wrong MARK cannot tell a
* broken SWITCH from a table that never carried the value.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131A
USE RSPT
? "RSE_G0_fixture_a_reads_AAA:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
CLOSE
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131B
USE RSPT
? "RSE_G1_fixture_b_reads_BBB:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
CLOSE
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
SET PATH DBF DBF
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE OWNER'S SANCTIONED SEQUENCE, TWICE: NEW / SWITCH / SET PATH / OPEN.
WORKSPACE NEW RSEWSA
WORKSPACE SWITCH RSEWSA
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131A
USE RSPT
? "RSE_G2_workspace_a_opened_its_own_table:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
WORKSPACE NEW RSEWSB
WORKSPACE SWITCH RSEWSB
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131B
USE RSPT
? "RSE_G3_workspace_b_opened_its_own_table:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
* RSE_T1 -- THE DISCRIMINATOR. Switch back to A and open WITHOUT setting the
* path again. Under the fix A's slots are restored and RSPT reads AAA. Before
* it, the DBF slot is still B's, the SAME FILENAME opens out of the wrong root,
* and this reads .F. -- a printed red, not a silence.
WORKSPACE SWITCH RSEWSA
USE RSPT
? "RSE_T1_switch_restored_this_workspace_environment:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
* RSE_T2 -- and the other direction, so a fix that simply pinned the slots to
* the first workspace cannot pass. Same shape, opposite expected value.
WORKSPACE SWITCH RSEWSB
USE RSPT
? "RSE_T2_switch_restores_the_other_way_too:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* RSE_T3/T4 -- Q1's EXPLICIT CLAUSE. Standing in B, bind A's DBF root with
* IN. Two claims, and both are needed: the session must NOT move (T3), and the
* binding must have actually landed on A (T4, proven by switching to A and
* opening without a SET PATH).
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131A IN RSEWSA
* CLOSE FIRST OR T3 IS BLIND -- MEASURED 2026-08-29 on build 008e7cd2. Without
* it the USE below answered "already open in current area 0": T2 had left B's
* table sitting in area 0, the USE declined to open, and the marker read BBB
* off a cursor the IN clause never touched. It would have read .T. whether or
* not the clause wrongly moved the session slot -- the arm could not go red.
* That is the AIF-148 shape this file's own header warns about, and T3 was the
* only USE here not preceded by a SWITCH or a CLOSE.
* A USE NOT PRECEDED BY A SWITCH OR A CLOSE IS NOT AN OPEN.
CLOSE
USE RSPT
? "RSE_T3_in_clause_left_the_session_alone:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
WORKSPACE SWITCH RSEWSA
USE RSPT
? "RSE_T4_in_clause_bound_the_named_workspace:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "AAA")
* RSE_T5 -- THE MISORDERING HAZARD R131 sec 7 exists to answer. Bind B's root
* to B while standing in A, using IN, then switch. Under the bare form this
* would have bound A -- the "NEW then SET PATH then SWITCH binds the OLD
* workspace" trap -- and the switch would then reopen A's table.
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131B IN RSEWSB
WORKSPACE SWITCH RSEWSB
USE RSPT
? "RSE_T5_explicit_binding_survived_the_switch:" + (ALLTRIM(MARK) = "BBB")
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* CLEANUP.
WORKSPACE CLOSE ALL
WORKSPACE DESTROY RSEWSA
WORKSPACE DESTROY RSEWSB
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131A
ERASE RSPT CONFIRM
SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX/R131B
ERASE RSPT CONFIRM
SET PATH DBF DBF
